    feat(text-stats): deliver the v0.2-run1 real-pipeline result with its evidence
    
    Run the real three-role pipeline once against the approved requirement text
    (v0.2-demo-input-3, R-01 - R-37) and keep its output exactly as produced:
    5 native subagent calls, 0 coding rework rounds, 76 delivery tests, 27 AC and
    27 BC items, final verdict APPROVED.
    
    Why this commit contains evidence and run records together with the code:
    the verdict is only meaningful next to the bytes it was produced from, so the
    six stage artifacts and the three run-record files (approval, precheck,
    injected requirement) are committed unchanged apart from the documented
    redaction of one local user path in precheck.json. `.gitattributes` pins those
    paths so that worktree bytes, Git blob bytes and the recorded sha256 stay
    identical on any machine.
    
    tests/review-run-evidence.py is the orchestrator-side re-check: it recomputes
    the artifact hashes from disk, verifies claim fields, ID uniqueness, review
    coverage and stage ordering, and classifies tracked changes into delivery
    source (must stay inside the four allowed files) versus documentation status
    updates. It reports 50/50 here, but it is a check of evidence consistency, not
    a substitute for the human acceptance decision.

